       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose. That raises a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** A single dose is typically no more than 1,000 mg, and 850 mg is the usual per-dose ceiling with TID dosing.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, or another titration step\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note that you've verified the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
